# Riverpod State Management Patterns

## Provider Types and Usage

### 1. Provider (Simple Values)
```dart
// For simple values that don't change
final themeProvider = Provider<ThemeMode>((ref) => ThemeMode.system);

// For dependencies
final repositoryProvider = Provider<Repository>((ref) {
  final box = ref.watch(hiveBoxProvider);
  return RepositoryImpl(box);
});
```

### 2. StateNotifierProvider (Complex State)
```dart
// For state that can change over time
final themeNotifierProvider = StateNotifierProvider<ThemeNotifier, ThemeMode>((ref) {
  return ThemeNotifier();
});

// Always extend BaseStateNotifier
class ThemeNotifier extends BaseStateNotifier<ThemeMode> {
  ThemeNotifier() : super(ThemeMode.system);
  
  void setTheme(ThemeMode mode) {
    updateState(mode);
  }
}
```

### 3. StreamProvider (Reactive Data)
```dart
// For streams of data
final allTransactionsProvider = StreamProvider<List<Transaction>>((ref) {
  final repository = ref.watch(transactionRepositoryProvider);
  return repository.watchAll();
});
```

### 4. Provider.family (Parameterized)
```dart
// For providers that depend on parameters
final transactionByIdProvider = Provider.family<Transaction?, String>((ref, id) {
  final repository = ref.watch(transactionRepositoryProvider);
  return repository.getById(id);
});
```

## Base Providers Pattern

Use [BaseProviders](mdc:lib/core/providers/base_providers.dart) for common patterns:

```dart
// Repository provider
final txRepositoryProvider = BaseProviders.repositoryProvider<TransactionRepoImpl, TransactionEntity>(
  (ref) => TransactionRepoImpl(ref.watch(txBoxProvider)),
);

// All entities stream
final allTransactionsProvider = BaseProviders.allEntitiesProvider<TransactionEntity>(
  txRepositoryProvider,
);

// Entity by ID
final transactionByIdProvider = BaseProviders.entityByIdProvider<TransactionEntity>(
  txRepositoryProvider,
);
```

## Form State Management

### BaseFormState Pattern
```dart
class TransactionFormState extends BaseFormState {
  final TransactionData data;
  
  const TransactionFormState({
    super.isLoading,
    super.isValid,
    super.error,
    super.fieldErrors,
    this.data = const TransactionData(),
  });
  
  @override
  TransactionFormState copyWith({
    bool? isLoading,
    bool? isValid,
    String? error,
    Map<String, String>? fieldErrors,
    TransactionData? data,
  }) {
    return TransactionFormState(
      isLoading: isLoading ?? this.isLoading,
      isValid: isValid ?? this.isValid,
      error: error ?? this.error,
      fieldErrors: fieldErrors ?? this.fieldErrors,
      data: data ?? this.data,
    );
  }
}
```

### BaseFormNotifier Pattern
```dart
class TransactionFormNotifier extends BaseFormNotifier<TransactionFormState> {
  TransactionFormNotifier() : super(TransactionFormState.initial());
  
  void updateAmount(double amount) {
    state = state.copyWith(
      data: state.data.copyWith(amount: amount),
    );
    validateForm();
  }
  
  @override
  void validateForm() {
    // Custom validation logic
    final isValid = state.data.amount > 0;
    state = state.copyWith(isValid: isValid);
  }
}
```

## Provider Organization

### File Structure
```
features/[feature]/presentation/viewmodels/
├── [feature]_providers.dart      # Main providers
├── [feature]_form_notifier.dart  # Form state management
└── [feature]_usecases_providers.dart # Use case providers
```

### Provider Naming
- Repository: `[feature]RepositoryProvider`
- State Notifier: `[feature]NotifierProvider`
- Stream: `all[Feature]sProvider`
- By ID: `[feature]ByIdProvider`
- Form: `[feature]FormNotifierProvider`

## State Notifier Best Practices

### 1. Extend BaseStateNotifier
```dart
class FeatureNotifier extends BaseStateNotifier<FeatureState> {
  FeatureNotifier() : super(FeatureState.initial());
  
  // Use updateState for safe state updates
  void updateFeature(Feature feature) {
    updateState(state.copyWith(feature: feature));
  }
}
```

### 2. Handle Async Operations
```dart
Future<void> loadData() async {
  await handleAsyncOperation(
    () async {
      final data = await repository.getAll();
      state = state.copyWith(data: data);
    },
    onError: (error) {
      state = state.copyWith(error: error.toString());
    },
  );
}
```

### 3. Use LoadingStateMixin
```dart
class FeatureNotifier extends BaseStateNotifier<FeatureState> 
    with LoadingStateMixin<FeatureState> {
  
  Future<void> loadData() async {
    setLoading(true);
    try {
      final data = await repository.getAll();
      state = state.copyWith(data: data);
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
    }
  }
}
```

## Consumer Widgets

### 1. Consumer (Basic)
```dart
class MyWidget extends ConsumerWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final theme = ref.watch(themeProvider);
    return Container(color: theme.primaryColor);
  }
}
```

### 2. ConsumerStatefulWidget (Complex)
```dart
class MyWidget extends ConsumerStatefulWidget {
  @override
  ConsumerState<MyWidget> createState() => _MyWidgetState();
}

class _MyWidgetState extends ConsumerState<MyWidget> {
  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    // Initialize with ref
    ref.read(provider.notifier).initialize();
  }
  
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final state = ref.watch(provider);
    return Container();
  }
}
```

### 3. Selector (Performance)
```dart
class MyWidget extends ConsumerWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final isLoading = ref.watch(
      featureProvider.select((state) => state.isLoading),
    );
    return isLoading ? CircularProgressIndicator() : Content();
  }
}
```

## Error Handling in Providers

### 1. Use Result Pattern
```dart
final dataProvider = FutureProvider<Result<Data>>((ref) async {
  try {
    final data = await repository.getData();
    return Ok(data);
  } catch (e) {
    return Err(DataFailure(e.toString()));
  }
});
```

### 2. Handle Provider Errors
```dart
Consumer(
  builder: (context, ref, child) {
    final result = ref.watch(dataProvider);
    return result.when(
      data: (result) => result.when(
        ok: (data) => DataWidget(data),
        err: (failure) => ErrorWidget(failure.message),
      ),
      loading: () => CircularProgressIndicator(),
      error: (error, stack) => ErrorWidget(error.toString()),
    );
  },
)
```

## Performance Optimization

### 1. Use autoDispose for Temporary Providers
```dart
final temporaryProvider = Provider.autoDispose((ref) {
  // This provider will be disposed when not used
  return TemporaryData();
});
```

### 2. Use select for Granular Rebuilds
```dart
// Only rebuild when specific field changes
final isLoading = ref.watch(
  featureProvider.select((state) => state.isLoading),
);
```

### 3. Use Provider.family for Cached Results
```dart
final cachedProvider = Provider.family.autoDispose<Data, String>((ref, id) {
  // Results are cached per id
  return repository.getById(id);
});
```

## Testing Providers

### 1. Mock Providers
```dart
final mockRepositoryProvider = Provider<Repository>((ref) => MockRepository());

testWidgets('should display data', (tester) async {
  await tester.pumpWidget(
    ProviderScope(
      overrides: [
        repositoryProvider.overrideWithValue(mockRepositoryProvider),
      ],
      child: MyWidget(),
    ),
  );
});
```

### 2. Test State Changes
```dart
test('should update state when data loads', () async {
  final container = ProviderContainer();
  final notifier = container.read(featureNotifierProvider.notifier);
  
  await notifier.loadData();
  
  expect(container.read(featureNotifierProvider).data, isNotNull);
});
```